# Cloudflare deploy

Two Workers ship from this repo: the **web** app (`apps/web`, Next.js via OpenNext: the Payload admin, its API and the public site) and the **cron** Worker (`apps/cron`, Hono: the daily backup). Both bind the same D1 database (`DB`). `web` binds the media bucket (`STORAGE`, and `NEXT_INC_CACHE_R2_BUCKET` for the page cache); `cron` binds the backups bucket (`BACKUPS`) and nothing else of R2.

Nothing in this repo reaches your Cloudflare account unless you ask for it: `dev`, `build`, `build:cf` and `preview` run on local D1 and R2 state, and only the commands below that say "remote" or "deploy" use your login.

**The Workers Paid plan is needed in practice.** The Free plan allows 10 ms of CPU per request and 50 D1 queries per invocation, which an admin request exceeds.

## One-time provisioning

{{> cloudflare/d1-provisioning}}

`apps/web/wrangler.jsonc` lists `PAYLOAD_SECRET` and `PREVIEW_SECRET` under `secrets.required`, and `apps/cron/wrangler.jsonc` lists `BACKUP_TRIGGER_TOKEN`: a deploy fails until each is set. The first deploy below sets them; afterwards change one with `{{#inDirectory "apps" "web"}}{{installedBinaryRunner}} wrangler secret put PAYLOAD_SECRET{{/inDirectory}}`.

## Production URL and first deploy

{{> blueprints/cloudflare-payload-nextjs/deploy}}

`robots.txt` disallows everything on a `workers.dev` address and on `localhost`, so the site is not indexed until it is served from a custom domain: set that domain as `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` for the build.

